hadiths[27]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17690","'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from 'Uthman ibn Hakim, who said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed me, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, who said: I saw three things from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which no one saw before me nor will anyone see after me. I went out with him on a journey until, when we were on part of the road, we passed a woman sitting with a boy of hers. She said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a boy afflicted with trial, and we were afflicted by him with trial; he is seized in the day I do not know how many times. He said: Hand him to me. She lifted him to him, and he placed him between himself and the middle of the saddle. Then he opened his mouth, blew into it three times, and said: In the name of Allah, I am the servant of Allah, be gone, enemy of Allah. Then he handed him back to her and said: Meet us on the return in this place and tell us what he did. He said: We went and returned, and found her in that place with three sheep. He said: What did your boy do? She said: By Him Who sent you with the truth, we have sensed nothing from him until this hour, so take these sheep. He said: Dismount and take one of them and return the rest. He said: I went out one day to the cemetery until, when we emerged, he said: Look, woe to you, do you see anything to conceal me? I said: I see nothing to conceal you except a tree which I do not think will conceal you. He said: What is near it? I said: A tree like it or close to it. He said: Go to them and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to join together by the permission of Allah. He said: They joined, and he relieved himself. Then he returned and said: Go to them and say to them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you that each of you return to its place. So it returned. He said: I was sitting with him one day when a camel came hurrying until it placed its chin before him, then its eyes shed tears. He said: Woe to you, look for whom this camel belongs; it has a matter. He said: I went out seeking its owner and found it belonging to a man from the Ansar. I called him to him, and he said: What is the matter with your camel? He said: What is its matter? He said: I do not know, by Allah, what is its matter; we worked on it and drew water on it until it became incapable of drawing water, so we decided last night to slaughter it and divide its meat. He said: Do not do it; give it to me or sell it to me. He said: Rather it is yours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He branded it with the brand of charity, then sent it forth."
"17691","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, from his father. Waki' said: Murrah, meaning al-Thaqafi, and he did not say Murrah from his father, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a boy of hers afflicted with madness. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Come out, enemy of Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah. He said: He recovered, and she gifted him two rams, something of dried yogurt, and something of ghee. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the dried yogurt and the ghee and one of the rams, and return the other to her."
"17692","Waki' narrated to us: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Ya'la al-Thaqafi, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood for prayer, would wipe the faces of his companions before he said takbir. I got some khaluq perfume on me, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped the faces of his companions and left me. He said: I returned and washed it, then came to the next prayer. He wiped my face and said: He returned with the good of his religion; the Most High has accepted repentance, and the sky has poured forth."
"17693","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: al-Mas'udi informed us, from Ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe our faces in prayer and bless us. He said: He came one day and wiped the faces of those on my right and my left and left me, and that was because I had entered upon a sister of mine and wiped my face with some yellow color. It was said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left you only because of what he saw on your face. I went to a well, entered it, and washed. Then I attended another prayer, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me, wiped my face, blessed me, and said: He returned with the good of his religion; the Most High has accepted repentance, and the sky has poured forth."
"17694","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu 'Amr ibn Hafs, or Abu Hafs ibn 'Amr, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw khaluq perfume on me and said: Do you have a wife? He said: I said: No. He said: Go and wash it, then do not repeat."
"17695","'Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Hafs ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with traces of saffron on me. He said: Wash it, then wash it, then wash it, then do not repeat. He said: I washed it, then I did not repeat."
"17696","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Hafs ibn 'Abd Allah, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with yellow saffron on me. He said: Wash it, then wash it, then do not repeat. He said: I washed it, then I did not repeat."
"17697","He narrated to us."
"17698","'Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us: 'Umar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Ya'la ibn Murrah, who said: I washed and perfumed myself with khaluq, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe our faces. When he drew near me, he kept his hand away from the khaluq. When he finished, he said: O Ya'la, what prompted you to use khaluq? Have you married? I said: No. He said to me: Go and wash it. He said: I passed a well, plunged into it, then rubbed myself with dust until it went away. He said: Then I came to him, and when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me, he said: He returned with the good of his religion; the Most High has accepted repentance, and the sky has poured forth."
"17699","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth narrated to us: al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Amr ibn 'Uthman Ya'la ibn Murrah al-Thaqafi, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a huge gold ring. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you pay zakat on this? He said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the zakat of this? When the man turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A great ember upon him."
"17700","'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, 'Abd Allah said: And I heard it from 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from 'Abd Allah ibn Hafs, from Ya'la ibn Murrah, that he was sitting with Ziyad when a man was brought who testified then changed his testimony. He said: I will surely cut your tongue. Ya'la said to him: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: Do not mutilate My servants. He said: So he left him."
"17701","Ismail ibn Muhammad, and he is Abu Ibrahim al-Muaqqib, narrated to us, Marwan, meaning al-Fazari, narrated to us, Abu Yafur narrated to us, from Abu Thabit who said: I heard Yala ibn Murra al-Thaqafi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever takes land without its right will be made to carry its soil to the place of gathering."
"17702","Abu Salama al-Khuzai narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Habib ibn Abi Jubayra, from Yala ibn Siyaba who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey of his, and he wanted to relieve himself, so he ordered two small palm shoots and one of them joined the other, then he ordered them and they returned to their planting places. And a camel came and struck its jowl to the ground, then it bellowed until what was around it became wet. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what the camel says. It claims that its owner intends to slaughter it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for him and said: Will you give him to me. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no wealth dearer to me than him. He said: Treat him well. He said: Of course, I shall not honor any wealth of mine with his honor, O Messenger of Allah. And he came upon a grave whose occupant was being punished, and he said: He is being punished for no great matter. So he ordered a palm stalk and it was placed upon his grave, and he said: Perhaps it will be lightened for him so long as it remains moist."
"17703","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Habib ibn Abi Jubayra, from Yala ibn Siyaba, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave and said: The occupant of this grave is being punished for no great matter. Then he called for a palm stalk and placed it upon his grave, and said: Perhaps it will be lightened for him so long as it remains moist."
"17704","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Rashid, from Yala al-Amiri, that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to a meal to which they had been invited. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went ahead. Affan said: Wuhayb said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced the front of the people, and Husayn was with boys playing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to take him. He said: The boy kept dodging here once and here once, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept laughing with him until he took him. He said: He placed one of his hands under his nape and the other under his chin, and placed his mouth upon his mouth and kissed him, and said: Husayn is from me and I am from Husayn. May Allah love whoever loves Husayn. Husayn is a sibt among the asbat."
"17705","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Rashid, from Yala al-Amiri, that Hasan and Husayn, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both, came racing to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he embraced them to himself and said: A child is a cause of miserliness and cowardice. And the last foothold that the Most Merciful, Almighty and Majestic, set was at Wajj."
"17706","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Yala ibn Murra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a woman brought him a son of hers who had been seized by madness, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Come out, O enemy of Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah. He said: So he recovered, and she gave him two rams and some dried yogurt and clarified butter. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Yala, take the dried yogurt and the clarified butter, and take one of the two rams, and return the other to her. And Waki once said: from his father, and he did not say: O Yala."
"17707","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Yala ibn Murra, from his father who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he stopped at a lodging place and said to me: Go to those two acacia trees and say to them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) orders you to come together. So I went to them and said that to them, and one of them leapt to the other and they came together. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and screened himself with them and relieved himself, then each one of them leapt back to its place."
"17708","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abdullah ibn Hafs, from Yala ibn Murra al-Thaqafi who said: Three things I saw from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). While we were traveling with him we passed by a camel used for drawing water, and when the camel saw him it bellowed and put its jowl down. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped by it and said: Where is the owner of this camel. So he came and he said: Sell it to me. He said: No, rather I give it to you as a gift. He said: No, sell it to me. He said: No, rather I give it to you as a gift, and it belongs to a household that has no livelihood besides it. He said: Since you have mentioned this about its affair, it has complained of much work and little fodder, so treat it well. He said: Then we traveled and stopped at a lodging place, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept, and a tree came splitting the earth until it covered him, then it returned to its place. When he awoke I mentioned it to him, and he said: It is a tree that asked permission of its Lord, Almighty and Majestic, to greet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and He permitted it. He said: Then we traveled and passed by water, and a woman brought him a son of hers afflicted with madness. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him by his nostril and said: Come out, indeed I am Muhammad the Messenger of Allah. He said: Then we traveled, and when we returned from our journey we passed by that water, and the woman brought him a slaughter camel and milk. He ordered her to return the slaughter camel, and he ordered his companions and they drank of the milk. He asked her about the boy, and she said: By Him who sent you with the truth, we have seen no trouble from him after you."
"17709","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Israil ibn Yunus informed us, Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Yala narrated to me, from his grandmother Hukayma, from her father Yala. Yazid said in what Yala ibn Murra narrates. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever picks up a small lost item, a dirham or a rope or the like, let him announce it for three days, and if it is above that, let him announce it for six days."
"17710","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Amra, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Yala who said: I do not think anyone among the people saw from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but less than what I saw. Then he mentioned the matter of the boy and the two palm trees and the matter of the camel, except that he said: What is with your camel complaining of you. It claims that you work it until when it grew old you intend to slaughter it. He said: You have spoken the truth, by Him who sent you with the truth as a Prophet, I had intended that, and by Him who sent you with the truth, I shall not do it."
"17711","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Yala ibn Murra al-Thaqafi who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Almighty and Majestic, said: Do not mutilate My servants."
"17712","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abu Yafur Abd al-Rahman, my grandfather, narrated to us, Abu Thabit narrated to us who said: I heard Yala ibn Murra al-Thaqafi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever takes land without its right will be made to carry its soil to the place of gathering."
"17713","Ubayda ibn Humayd narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to me, from a man called Abdullah ibn Hafs, from Yala ibn Murra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me while I was perfumed with khaluq, and he said to me: O Yala, what is this khaluq. Do you have a wife. He said: I said: No. He said: Go and wash it off yourself, then wash it, then wash it, and do not return."
"17714","Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaida, from al-Rabi ibn Abdullah, from Ayman ibn Nabil, from Yala ibn Murra who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any man who wrongs a handspan of land, Allah, Almighty and Majestic, will make him dig it until he reaches the last of the seven earths, then He will yoke it upon him until the Day of Resurrection until judgment is passed among the people."
"17715","Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib who said: I heard Abu Hafs ibn Amr, or Abu Amr ibn Hafs al-Thaqafi who said: I heard Yala ibn Murra al-Thaqafi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me perfumed and said: Do you have a wife. I said: No. He said: Wash it, then wash it, then wash it, and do not return."
"17716","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Umar ibn Maymun ibn al-Rammah narrated to us, from Abu Sahl Kathir ibn Ziyad al-Basri, from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Yala ibn Murra, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a narrow pass, he and his companions, while he was upon his mount, with the sky above them and wet ground beneath them. Prayer came due, so he ordered the caller to prayer and he called the adhan and the iqama. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advanced upon his mount and prayed with them, gesturing with gestures, making prostration lower than bowing, or making his prostration lower than his bowing."
